Run the profiling forward pass once before the measured one and release the allocator's cached blocks between them, so a cold compile cache does not land torch.compile and Triton JIT scratch inside the memory-profiling window.

Measured on 0.29.0: on a fresh cache volume the profiled transient peak read 0.95 GiB above the warm boot's (WSL2 RTX 4090 and native RTX 3090, GPU_UTIL 0.90), and the KV-memory check refused the default 65,536-token profile (4.73 GiB available against 4.76 needed) and the KVarN profile (available read as -1.86 GiB); the same boot on a warm cache passed. 0.28.0 did not show it. The pinned-pool path (kv_cache_memory_bytes) already runs one uncounted profile_run and is unchanged.

